---
import ReportLayout from '../layouts/ReportLayout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../components/report/StatusPill.astro';
import { parts } from '../data/parts';
---
<ReportLayout title="Hardware" description="The current v2 sensor direction and the archived v0.1 prototype hardware.">
  <section class="report-container py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">Current hardware · v0.2</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><h1 class="text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">Sensor and carrier board</h1><StatusPill state="in review" /></div>
    <div class="prose prose-site mt-10 max-w-[75ch] prose-headings:font-display prose-p:leading-8">
      <p>The current direction is a small USB desk-height sensor: an RP2040-Zero reads a VL53L0X time-of-flight sensor over I2C and sends readings to the computer over USB Serial. The computer owns presence inference, the decision loop and notifications.</p>
      <p>This hardware does not control the desk motor and does not contain mains wiring. The user still presses the desk's own button.</p>
      <p>E003 contains a generated review pack for four candidate board variants. Local contract and artifact checks pass, but that is not fabrication approval.</p>
      <h2>Open review gates</h2>
      <ul><li>Capture calibrated dimensions and pad maps for the received modules.</li><li>Characterize the breakout power rail, I2C voltage domain and pull-ups.</li><li>Shorten and inspect the routing with explicit layer intent.</li><li>Obtain a qualified external electronics review.</li></ul>
      <p><a href="/updates/2026-09-02-pcb-v2-carrier-board" class="report-link">Read the PCB v2 design brief</a> or see the <a href="/versions" class="report-link">version log</a> for the architectural decision behind this direction.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="report-container pb-16 md:pb-20">
    <div class="mb-8"><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">Archived hardware · v0.1 / v0.1.1</p><h2 class="text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">The first integrated prototype</h2></div>
    <div class="prose prose-site max-w-[75ch] prose-headings:font-display prose-p:leading-8"><p>The original control unit combined a Raspberry Pi, relay board, laser distance sensor, PIR presence sensor, power supply and a physical controller. Version 0.1.1 replaced the original power supply with a smaller one. This is historical material, not the current hardware recommendation.</p><p><a href="/updates/2026-09-02-v0-1-first-smart-desk-prototype" class="report-link">Read the complete v0.1 build report</a>.</p></div>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{['plexi-cutted.jpg', 'wiring.jpg', 'wiring-explained.jpg', '20230628_032916.jpg', '20230628_033107.jpg', '20230628_033525.jpg', '20230628_033548.jpg', '20230628_033806.jpg', '20230628_043425.jpg'].map((image) => <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface"><img src={`/images/${image}`} alt={`Archived v0.1 hardware: ${image}`} loading="lazy" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover" /><figcaption class="p-3 text-xs text-ink-muted">Archived v0.1 hardware · {image}</figcaption></figure>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="report-container pb-16 md:pb-20">
    <div class="mb-8"><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">v0.1 bill of materials</p><h2 class="text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">What the first prototype used</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-ink-muted">The list below is preserved for reproducibility and historical context. It includes mains-related parts; do not treat it as a build guide for v0.2.</p></div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">{parts.map((part) => <article class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface"><img src={part.img.startsWith('images/') ? `/${part.img}` : part.img} alt={part.name} loading="lazy" class="h-32 w-full object-contain bg-white p-2" /><div class="p-4"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold leading-5 text-ink">{part.name}</h3>{part.priceValue && <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted">Historical estimate: {part.priceValue} {part.currency}</p>}{part.url && <a href={part.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="report-link mt-3 inline-block text-xs">Reference</a>}</div></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="report-container pb-20">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8"><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-text">Archive files</p><h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Original v0.1 enclosure</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-ink-muted">The DXF files describe the historical laser-cut plexiglass enclosure. The design is not recommended as-is because the original enclosure did not provide adequate airflow.</p><div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-4"><a class="report-link text-sm" href="/enclosure/v1/plexi_5mm_40x20cm.dxf">Download 5 mm enclosure DXF</a><a class="report-link text-sm" href="/enclosure/v1/plexi_smoked_graphite_3mm_9x13.5cm.dxf">Download smoked plexiglass DXF</a></div></div>
  </section>
</ReportLayout>
